From 459a03998463fcf22ab7b62ea56190dbbf7351dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <agent@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:28:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: fix AMeter calibration EEPROM record stride

The merged 0126 AMeter EEPROM filled six 8-byte calibration records at
208 + gain*16, but the executable driver reads them at 208 + gain*8
(PAG_6144/4096/.../256_CAL_ADDR). Loading the PGA_256 record therefore
returned zeros, the synthetic CRC matched a zero record, and the driver's
set_gain() divided expect/real = 0/0, so AMeterUnit could not be constructed
in guest evidence.

Use the driver's 8-byte stride and keep the same synthetic factor-1.0 record
(expect=real=1000). No other AMeter semantics changed.
---
 hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_sensors.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_sensors.c b/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_sensors.c
index 7586d97..a17d0c4 100644
--- a/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_sensors.c
+++ b/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_sensors.c
@@ -358,8 +358,12 @@ static void ameter_config_get(Object *obj, Visitor *v, const char *name,
  * NOT a real factory calibration. */
 static void ameter_fill_eeprom(M5UnitSensor *s)
 {
+    /* The official driver reads the per-gain calibration record at
+     * 208 + gain * 8 (PAG_*_CAL_ADDR), not at a 16-byte stride. The merged
+     * 0126 used stride 16, so PGA_256 read a zero record and the driver's
+     * set_gain() divided by zero (expect/real). */
     for (unsigned gain = 0; gain < 6; gain++) {
-        uint8_t *r = s->regs[0] + 208 + gain * 16;
+        uint8_t *r = s->regs[0] + 208 + gain * 8;
         r[0] = gain;
         r[1] = 0x03; r[2] = 0xe8;   /* expect = 1000 */
         r[3] = 0x03; r[4] = 0xe8;   /* real   = 1000 */
